SOAPBOX: Thank you, everyone! I had actually never run an RTTY contest
SOAPBOX: from my own QTH before, only from big contest stations like SZ1A
SOAPBOX: or J42L, where everything is already perfectly set up. This
SOAPBOX: weekend I was in Skopje, and I spent days struggling to get my
SOAPBOX: own rig configured properly. I even started the contest with an
SOAPBOX: AFSK setup, a fair amount of ignorance, and a long list of
SOAPBOX: issues.
SOAPBOX: DL1NM's excellent document, did everything finally click. I
SOAPBOX: switched to FSK, exactly the way I had always assumed it should
SOAPBOX: work, and from that moment on everything made sense. I enjoyed
SOAPBOX: the contest immensely, and I came out of it both satisfied and
SOAPBOX: wiser. Thank you very much, dear Gerd! His message is available
SOAPBOX: here: https://groups.io/g/MMTTY-SB-RTTY/message/1255
